  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 21.5, p. 399. Book: EFL 100, BFL -0.004675, NA -0.664 (F/0.75), GIH 10.51 (HFOV=6.00), PTZ/F -5.183, VL 183.01, infinite conjugate. Wavelengths 10.6, 8, 13 um as in the book (primary first). Glass: CSI entered as 1.739 (constant index: no cesium iodide dispersion data in the catalogs, so its color is not modelled); GERMA entered as GERMANIUM (Zemax INFRARED catalog); ZNSIR entered as ZNS_BROAD (zinc sulfide, Zemax INFRARED catalog). The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the front surface, whose semi-aperture matches the axial beam (the book does not mark the stop). Infrared materials come from the Zemax INFRARED catalog; the book lists their indices at the primary wavelength from older data, so small differences in EFL are expected. The last element is a plane zinc sulfide window just ahead of the image.",
